UPDATE "QuestionBankItem" SET scenario = $s0$A 28-year-old woman is evaluated for a fasting plasma glucose of 118 mg/dL on two separate mornings. Her hemoglobin A1c is 6.4%. She is lean, has no polyuria, and has never had ketoacidosis. Her mother and maternal grandfather have had the same mild fasting hyperglycemia since early adulthood and have never needed insulin. Glutamic acid decarboxylase antibodies are negative.$s0$, explanation = $e0$This is maturity-onset diabetes of the young from a glucokinase (GCK) variant: lifelong mild fasting hyperglycemia, a similarly affected parent and grandparent, no ketoacidosis, and negative islet antibodies. Glucokinase sets the glucose threshold for insulin release. Phosphofructokinase, hexokinase, and fructose-1,6-bisphosphatase defects do not produce this stable autosomal-dominant fasting pattern.$e0$, "references" = $r0$[{"label": "MedlinePlus Genetics. GCK-MODY is a mild form of maturity-onset diabetes of the young, with slightly high fasting blood glucose.", "url": "https://medlineplus.gov/genetics/condition/maturity-onset-diabetes-of-the-young/"}]$r0$::jsonb, "contentHash" = '3bec3c39c62761bfcf5b81a34d079ad1583a96ac1b997c47c179a3751a19adb4', manual_correction = true, "generationMeta" = CASE WHEN "generationMeta" IS NULL THEN '{"manualCorrection": true}'::jsonb WHEN jsonb_typeof("generationMeta")='object' THEN jsonb_set("generationMeta", '{manualCorrection}', 'true'::jsonb, true) ELSE "generationMeta" END, "updatedAt" = NOW()
WHERE id = 'cmr89b4oc00kj1yw2ydxc7lrf' AND "contentHash" = '1cbd3aba198451d16b8e7a5b2fb782220a1712e5bf79cd4ed9ef4fe4e3c5fca2';
UPDATE "QuestionBankItem" SET scenario = $s1$A 28-year-old woman presents to the emergency department with a 2-day history of recurrent seizures. She has epilepsy treated with oxcarbazepine. She is confused. She has been taking the medicine as prescribed. Vital signs are stable. No laboratory values are provided in the chart yet.$s1$, question = $q1$Which laboratory finding is the most likely cause of these breakthrough seizures?$q1$, explanation = $e1$Oxcarbazepine commonly lowers the serum sodium. Hyponatremia lowers the seizure threshold. The stem does not give a sodium value. Creatinine, potassium, and liver enzymes are not the usual oxcarbazepine effect that provokes seizures.$e1$, "contentHash" = '53a44b9e77acf76de836ca645b07ab94b95e01ed98fd91646048ec7831c874f7', manual_correction = true, "generationMeta" = CASE WHEN "generationMeta" IS NULL THEN '{"manualCorrection": true}'::jsonb WHEN jsonb_typeof("generationMeta")='object' THEN jsonb_set("generationMeta", '{manualCorrection}', 'true'::jsonb, true) ELSE "generationMeta" END, "updatedAt" = NOW()
WHERE id = 'cmr8ei2tu00a21yazj9fki812' AND "contentHash" = '9c737dae6d8ae74d26dc3df00ab82efe9122b8d24fc48c508944b720ce98e08d';
UPDATE "QuestionBankItem" SET scenario = $s2$A 68-year-old man is admitted to the emergency department with acute respiratory distress. He has a history of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) and is currently on a bronchodilator. On examination, he is tachypneic with a respiratory rate of 28 breaths per minute and an oxygen saturation of 88% on room air. Arterial blood gas analysis reveals a pH of 7.30, PaCO2 of 60 mmHg, and PaO2 of 55 mmHg. He is wheezing. The chest radiograph shows hyperinflation and no focal consolidation.$s2$, explanation = $e2$He has a COPD exacerbation: wheeze, hyperinflation without consolidation, hypoxemia, and CO2 retention. Airflow obstruction raises airway resistance and causes ventilation-perfusion mismatch. Bilateral inflammatory permeability and surfactant loss describe ARDS, which this radiograph does not show. Hypoventilation does not decrease pulmonary blood flow as the main mechanism here.$e2$, "contentHash" = '34588a2af05fc1dbdbe7fe74ce514fe25d87a082a0eb551f7bb7ecace708fdf7', manual_correction = true, "generationMeta" = CASE WHEN "generationMeta" IS NULL THEN '{"manualCorrection": true}'::jsonb WHEN jsonb_typeof("generationMeta")='object' THEN jsonb_set("generationMeta", '{manualCorrection}', 'true'::jsonb, true) ELSE "generationMeta" END, "updatedAt" = NOW()
WHERE id = 'cmrrum1cu00hi1y8wrru12a6s' AND "contentHash" = '2df62fa3d3fc722fd34bd94f72c933c4c7d1eed2c744ce6bef320c310e3c8f95';
UPDATE "QuestionBankItem" SET scenario = $s3$A 58-year-old woman with type 2 diabetes for 15 years and hypertension is seen because her creatinine has risen. She has had no acute illness. Blood pressure is 148/88 mm Hg. Fundoscopy shows retinal microaneurysms. Creatinine is 2.1 mg/dL, up from 1.4 mg/dL one year ago. Urinalysis shows 3+ protein and no red blood cells or casts.$s3$, explanation = $e3$Longstanding diabetes, retinopathy, a slow creatinine rise, and heavy proteinuria without hematuria or casts is diabetic nephropathy. Acute glomerulonephritis would show hematuria and red-cell casts over days. Hypertensive nephrosclerosis causes less proteinuria. 'Chronic kidney disease' names the stage, not the diabetic lesion.$e3$, "contentHash" = '986440c21ff178f0ab2b5e17fe5d9460c4be3197192ec5776401f5d30c328c17', manual_correction = true, "generationMeta" = CASE WHEN "generationMeta" IS NULL THEN '{"manualCorrection": true}'::jsonb WHEN jsonb_typeof("generationMeta")='object' THEN jsonb_set("generationMeta", '{manualCorrection}', 'true'::jsonb, true) ELSE "generationMeta" END, "updatedAt" = NOW()
WHERE id = 'cmrpvuy8z000v1yh5a2u8z3wc' AND "contentHash" = '17791a9ee05f65f1158fe3f6f64b189dc3db9a3142f514f571b84eeb81fe4b8b';
UPDATE "QuestionBankItem" SET scenario = $s4$A 45-year-old man with a history of hypertension and diabetes presents for a routine check-up. His laboratory results show a serum creatinine of 2.3 mg/dL and a blood urea nitrogen (BUN) of 30 mg/dL. He has not experienced any recent changes in medication or diet. His blood pressure is 150/90 mm Hg. Serum sodium is 140 mEq/L, chloride is 104 mEq/L, and bicarbonate is 24 mEq/L.$s4$, explanation = $e4$Anion gap = sodium − (chloride + bicarbonate) = 140 − (104 + 24) = 12 mEq/L. The gap is normal. The creatinine and urea do not enter this calculation.$e4$, "contentHash" = 'ae33453c7bd358f31a628316a364f7751065a6095ccf23bf1abbd0d0a69cf4a1', manual_correction = true, "generationMeta" = CASE WHEN "generationMeta" IS NULL THEN '{"manualCorrection": true}'::jsonb WHEN jsonb_typeof("generationMeta")='object' THEN jsonb_set("generationMeta", '{manualCorrection}', 'true'::jsonb, true) ELSE "generationMeta" END, "updatedAt" = NOW()
WHERE id = 'cmrr4t1u0000k1y6pg528ivkh' AND "contentHash" = 'caed44480f595b5c26cd3eb23aa896311d57599d8ad3dc5b436da013044e5e1b';
UPDATE "QuestionBankItem" SET scenario = $s5$A 55-year-old man presents with jaundice and fatigue that have developed over several months. He does not drink alcohol. AST is 70 U/L and ALT is 150 U/L. Hepatitis C antibody is positive and hepatitis C RNA is detected. Ultrasound shows no biliary dilation and no gallstones.$s5$, "correctAnswer" = $k5$Chronic inflammation leading to fibrosis$k5$, explanation = $e5$Chronic hepatitis C injures the liver through persistent inflammation that leads to fibrosis. He does not drink, the ALT is higher than the AST, and the bile ducts are not blocked. Direct viral cytotoxicity is not the main mechanism of hepatitis C injury, and this is not autoimmune hepatitis.$e5$, "contentHash" = '028eb60fc157acbffb8d1fda40fc3d62d12362d691c7df0dd66c9f08ada9492d', manual_correction = true, "generationMeta" = CASE WHEN "generationMeta" IS NULL THEN '{"manualCorrection": true}'::jsonb WHEN jsonb_typeof("generationMeta")='object' THEN jsonb_set("generationMeta", '{manualCorrection}', 'true'::jsonb, true) ELSE "generationMeta" END, "updatedAt" = NOW()
WHERE id = 'cmrpw16sy002b1yh5v9azodfx' AND "contentHash" = 'ec8061bbe9fd1a0baa55274e7835ed9042289ff153751e05e1e9dd74d4912817';
UPDATE "QuestionBankItem" SET scenario = $s6$A 45-year-old man with a history of hypertension presents to the clinic for a routine check-up. He reports occasional headaches and blurred vision. His blood pressure is 160/100 mm Hg, and laboratory tests reveal a serum creatinine level of 1.5 mg/dL. A urinalysis shows mild proteinuria. An abdominal bruit is heard. The right kidney measures 8 cm and the left measures 11 cm. Creatinine rose from 1.1 to 1.6 mg/dL after lisinopril was started.$s6$, options = replace(options, $a6$Decreased renal blood flow$a6$, $b6$Primary aldosterone excess$b6$), explanation = $e6$A bruit, a small kidney, and a creatinine rise after an ACE inhibitor indicate renal artery stenosis. The underperfused kidney secretes renin, and angiotensin II raises the blood pressure. Primary aldosterone excess would suppress renin. Vascular compliance is not increased in this setting, and sympathetic tone is not the specific mechanism.$e6$, "contentHash" = '8b45557824da1f2f3bc566e34fb0b8c8e4cc8a1964a99493275bc7840f2e6e77', manual_correction = true, "generationMeta" = CASE WHEN "generationMeta" IS NULL THEN '{"manualCorrection": true}'::jsonb WHEN jsonb_typeof("generationMeta")='object' THEN jsonb_set("generationMeta", '{manualCorrection}', 'true'::jsonb, true) ELSE "generationMeta" END, "updatedAt" = NOW()
WHERE id = 'cmr89p24d00nb1yw2dp1cbdre' AND "contentHash" = 'c782a4435f233fe85e7bec4af00848db81f4f76a663b00831baa853abf98ec8d';
UPDATE "QuestionBankItem" SET explanation = $e7$She is not described as pregnant. A blood pressure of 180/110 mm Hg with headache, retinal hemorrhages, and proteinuria is a hypertensive emergency. The vessel injury is endothelial dysfunction with increased permeability. This is not preeclampsia. A primary surge in nitric oxide would lower, not raise, the blood pressure.$e7$, "references" = $r7$[{"label": "AHA highlights of the 2017 ACC/AHA guideline, Table 2. Hypertensive emergency is a systolic pressure above 180 mm Hg and/or a diastolic pressure above 120 mm Hg with new target-organ damage.", "url": "https://www.fmda.org/assets/docs/journal-club/Highlights-from-the-2017-Guideline.pdf"}]$r7$::jsonb, manual_correction = true, "generationMeta" = CASE WHEN "generationMeta" IS NULL THEN '{"manualCorrection": true}'::jsonb WHEN jsonb_typeof("generationMeta")='object' THEN jsonb_set("generationMeta", '{manualCorrection}', 'true'::jsonb, true) ELSE "generationMeta" END, "updatedAt" = NOW()
WHERE id = 'cmrth8bb2005g1yax15cu6j80' AND "contentHash" = '44a561ad90903915a80240e12eebd10ff44650768291d179898a7b903305125a';
UPDATE "QuestionBankItem" SET scenario = $s8$A 58-year-old man presents to the emergency department with palpitations and shortness of breath. He has a history of hypertension and is currently taking lisinopril. On examination, his blood pressure is 142/88 mm Hg, heart rate is 120 beats per minute, and he appears anxious. An ECG shows narrow QRS complexes with a regular rhythm. Laboratory tests reveal a potassium level of 4.1 mEq/L.$s8$, "correctAnswer" = $k8$Increased sympathetic stimulation$k8$, explanation = $e8$He is anxious, with a regular narrow-complex rate of 120 and a normal potassium. That is sinus tachycardia from sympathetic drive. Hyperkalemia raises extracellular, not intracellular, potassium and widens the QRS. Vagal tone is not decreased as the specific finding, and an isolated AV-node conduction change is not required for sinus tachycardia.$e8$, "references" = $r8$[{"label": "MedlinePlus Medical Encyclopedia. A high potassium level is a high level in the blood, and severe elevation affects the heart.", "url": "https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/001179.htm"}]$r8$::jsonb, "contentHash" = '02152f53fa07ff6933a4c89f29a2a82100bf370f38bb9cf6e6ffa4f7057dd468', manual_correction = true, "generationMeta" = CASE WHEN "generationMeta" IS NULL THEN '{"manualCorrection": true}'::jsonb WHEN jsonb_typeof("generationMeta")='object' THEN jsonb_set("generationMeta", '{manualCorrection}', 'true'::jsonb, true) ELSE "generationMeta" END, "updatedAt" = NOW()
WHERE id = 'cmr89zvio00q81yw2dehw8v84' AND "contentHash" = 'a52af3908f08f908c5ec0bd74f8542fa68a9576966d69caa0832c7c0901667dc';
UPDATE "QuestionBankItem" SET scenario = $s9$A 45-year-old woman presents to the emergency department with severe left shoulder pain and shortness of breath. She has a history of hypertension and hyperlipidemia and is a current smoker. On examination, her blood pressure is 150/90 mm Hg, heart rate is 110 bpm, and she has decreased breath sounds on the left side. Percussion is dull over the left base, and the chest radiograph shows blunting of the left costophrenic angle.$s9$, explanation = $e9$Dullness and blunting of the costophrenic angle are a pleural effusion. The radiograph does not name that diagnosis. Pneumothorax is hyper-resonant with a visible pleural line. Pulmonary embolism and myocardial infarction do not produce a large costophrenic blunting as the main finding.$e9$, "contentHash" = '58d611998481fd098969ddb17edaed6165e435a92b2ed1e288371cf1f59289f2', manual_correction = true, "generationMeta" = CASE WHEN "generationMeta" IS NULL THEN '{"manualCorrection": true}'::jsonb WHEN jsonb_typeof("generationMeta")='object' THEN jsonb_set("generationMeta", '{manualCorrection}', 'true'::jsonb, true) ELSE "generationMeta" END, "updatedAt" = NOW()
WHERE id = 'cmtpwsmza003r1y6hbfr6o1gh' AND "contentHash" = '35cb901b09e72aceb61c700c9c41651234baff89131b80943929da85ca621a9e';
UPDATE "QuestionBankItem" SET scenario = $s10$A 72-year-old woman with longstanding hypertension is brought in because her thinking has worsened in steps. She had a left hemiparesis two years ago and dysarthria eight months ago, and each time her memory was worse afterward. She is afebrile. Blood pressure is 168/96 mm Hg. CT shows several old lacunar infarcts and no mass or acute hemorrhage.$s10$, explanation = $e10$Stepwise cognitive loss after clinically evident strokes, with hypertension and old lacunes, is vascular dementia. Alzheimer disease is gradual and lacks this stroke history. Normal-pressure hydrocephalus is gait change, incontinence, and dementia without multiple infarcts. She is afebrile and the decline has been over years, so this is not delirium.$e10$, "contentHash" = '3232b1b4f6e03b49eb5fdd26aadf510506a8d77f9293a820134baa5c59e5bf93', manual_correction = true, "generationMeta" = CASE WHEN "generationMeta" IS NULL THEN '{"manualCorrection": true}'::jsonb WHEN jsonb_typeof("generationMeta")='object' THEN jsonb_set("generationMeta", '{manualCorrection}', 'true'::jsonb, true) ELSE "generationMeta" END, "updatedAt" = NOW()
WHERE id = 'cmr891ee800y41yr96l2sipc7' AND "contentHash" = '5e474b087c3f806e1ddaee2337eb8d0a06cd0e5f8594e734f809ebacfc6db7f4';
UPDATE "QuestionBankItem" SET scenario = $s11$A 30-year-old man has had fever, cough, and pleuritic chest pain for 3 days. He has no cancer, heart failure, liver disease, kidney disease, or stroke. He is alert. Temperature is 38.6°C, heart rate 96 beats per minute, respiratory rate 22 breaths per minute, and blood pressure 122/74 mm Hg. Oxygen saturation is 96% on room air. Blood urea nitrogen is 12 mg/dL, sodium is 138 mEq/L, and glucose is 98 mg/dL. Chest radiography shows a single right-lower-lobe opacity and no pleural effusion.$s11$, explanation = $e11$The Pneumonia Severity Index is the tool the 2019 ATS/IDSA guideline prefers over CURB-65 when deciding on hospitalization. His only points are his age (30). Risk class I–II is treated out of the hospital. He is not hypoxic, hypotensive, or confused, so oral antibiotics are appropriate and intravenous therapy, a culture-first delay, and thoracentesis are not.$e11$, "references" = $r11$[{"label": "ATS/IDSA 2019 guideline (PMC6812437). Use the Pneumonia Severity Index in preference to CURB-65 to decide whether an adult with community-acquired pneumonia needs hospitalization.", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6812437/"}]$r11$::jsonb, "contentHash" = 'ede6b55be0c4dc72ad1ba449c0b7c0dd10479eee85999b6d92d40e0b5898bf42', manual_correction = true, "generationMeta" = CASE WHEN "generationMeta" IS NULL THEN '{"manualCorrection": true}'::jsonb WHEN jsonb_typeof("generationMeta")='object' THEN jsonb_set("generationMeta", '{manualCorrection}', 'true'::jsonb, true) ELSE "generationMeta" END, "updatedAt" = NOW()
WHERE id = 'cmr891bwq00xf1yr9h77x9i2g' AND "contentHash" = '34c70cb8a24f08e089d355778db09918e6d0e60adbc7cb2563a5f08366cddf79';
UPDATE "QuestionBankItem" SET scenario = $s12$A 45-year-old woman presents to the emergency department with severe abdominal pain that started suddenly two hours ago. She has a history of hypertension and is currently on lisinopril. On examination, her blood pressure is 90/60 mm Hg, heart rate is 120 bpm, and she appears diaphoretic. Laboratory tests reveal elevated white blood cell count and elevated serum amylase. A CT scan shows a 3 cm gallstone in the common bile duct. She is afebrile and not jaundiced.$s12$, "correctAnswer" = $k12$Intravenous fluids and observation$k12$, explanation = $e12$Sudden pain, hypotension, a high amylase, and a common-bile-duct stone is gallstone pancreatitis. She has no fever and no jaundice, so she does not have cholangitis. Early ERCP is reserved for cholangitis or obstruction that does not clear. The immediate treatment is intravenous fluid. Cholecystectomy is later, and MRCP is unnecessary because CT already shows the stone.$e12$, "contentHash" = '6fc3b3c325b1651076a810efe6e15cec5a31893d88ce182f73758feadb82fd8c', manual_correction = true, "generationMeta" = CASE WHEN "generationMeta" IS NULL THEN '{"manualCorrection": true}'::jsonb WHEN jsonb_typeof("generationMeta")='object' THEN jsonb_set("generationMeta", '{manualCorrection}', 'true'::jsonb, true) ELSE "generationMeta" END, "updatedAt" = NOW()
WHERE id = 'cmrpw5xp0006w1ylu2a8o5cb4' AND "contentHash" = 'e9a0333bf448c7da4d24ed624ceb3dc3f46071d401849e0c687a1e5499eed0d3';
UPDATE "QuestionBankItem" SET scenario = $s13$A 54-year-old man with type 2 diabetes is brought to the emergency department because he is confused. He has been drinking very little. Mucous membranes are dry. Glucose is 780 mg/dL, sodium is 150 mEq/L, bicarbonate is 23 mEq/L, and serum osmolality is 345 mOsm/kg. Urine ketones are negative.$s13$, explanation = $e13$Extremely high glucose without ketones, dehydration, and decreased alertness is hyperosmolar hyperglycemic syndrome. Bicarbonate is 23 mEq/L, so this is not ketoacidosis. He is not hypoglycemic. The glucose of 780 with an osmolality of 345 is far beyond ordinary type 2 diabetes follow-up.$e13$, "references" = $r13$[{"label": "MedlinePlus Medical Encyclopedia. Hyperosmolar hyperglycemic syndrome is extremely high blood glucose without ketones, with dehydration and decreased alertness.", "url": "https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/000304.htm"}]$r13$::jsonb, "contentHash" = '3c282a6c5a05d5a3687dc51604e5288b57c00efeab8514857c512fa5be39f619', manual_correction = true, "generationMeta" = CASE WHEN "generationMeta" IS NULL THEN '{"manualCorrection": true}'::jsonb WHEN jsonb_typeof("generationMeta")='object' THEN jsonb_set("generationMeta", '{manualCorrection}', 'true'::jsonb, true) ELSE "generationMeta" END, "updatedAt" = NOW()
WHERE id = 'cmr98dkkz00h71ywywhzzbztp' AND "contentHash" = 'b57add0216c4715089f4d63bcf5ae8847bed70a180b137ce089401c250f4b7b7';
UPDATE "QuestionBankItem" SET scenario = $s14$A 32-year-old woman presents to the emergency department two weeks after a vaginal delivery. She reports increasing fatigue, palpitations, and shortness of breath on exertion. On examination, her blood pressure is 90/60 mm Hg, heart rate is 110 beats per minute, and she has a pale appearance. Laboratory tests reveal a hemoglobin level of 8.5 g/dL and a reticulocyte count of 5%. She is soaking more than one pad an hour and passing clots. The uterus is boggy.$s14$, explanation = $e14$Two weeks after delivery she is bleeding heavily, with a boggy uterus, hypotension, tachycardia, anemia, and a high reticulocyte count. That is delayed postpartum hemorrhage. Iron deficiency is a slower process and does not produce this acute bleed. Thrombotic thrombocytopenic purpura and gestational hypertension do not fit heavy vaginal bleeding with a boggy uterus.$e14$, "contentHash" = 'd0701c60292373df9f3245df57392fd34a7abb79212b8584254e144d2ef4ff7b', manual_correction = true, "generationMeta" = CASE WHEN "generationMeta" IS NULL THEN '{"manualCorrection": true}'::jsonb WHEN jsonb_typeof("generationMeta")='object' THEN jsonb_set("generationMeta", '{manualCorrection}', 'true'::jsonb, true) ELSE "generationMeta" END, "updatedAt" = NOW()
WHERE id = 'cmr8mlwcf00nv1ygitr6bbt4y' AND "contentHash" = '5e66243637deeacbd6c3af372f5aab3e3055a9600bd9869c93cb97b863bca523';
UPDATE "QuestionBankItem" SET scenario = $s15$A 62-year-old woman is admitted to the surgical ward following a laparoscopic cholecystectomy. On postoperative day 6, a port-site incision is red and draining pus, and her temperature is 101.5°F (38.6°C). Her vital signs are stable, with a blood pressure of 120/75 mm Hg and heart rate of 88 bpm. Laboratory tests reveal a white blood cell count of 12,000/mm³. She has no history of prior infections and is currently on IV fluids and analgesics.$s15$, explanation = $e15$Purulent drainage from the incision on day 6 is a surgical-site infection. Wound infections are uncommon on day 2, when atelectasis is the usual fever. She has no cough to support pneumonia, no urinary symptoms, and no leg swelling to support thrombosis.$e15$, "contentHash" = '8f4d436c6c07d6b8060e2433b5d5fc208dad712a14b91993b651343451932104', manual_correction = true, "generationMeta" = CASE WHEN "generationMeta" IS NULL THEN '{"manualCorrection": true}'::jsonb WHEN jsonb_typeof("generationMeta")='object' THEN jsonb_set("generationMeta", '{manualCorrection}', 'true'::jsonb, true) ELSE "generationMeta" END, "updatedAt" = NOW()
WHERE id = 'cmr8atvyl000t1ylomai0a6f3' AND "contentHash" = '123cb57a1ac90803554b2de549db2aa7fc354f12d3721dee0a15715696231cc6';
UPDATE "QuestionBankItem" SET "correctAnswer" = $k16$Stop lisinopril and discuss an ARB trial$k16$, options = replace(options, $a16$Discontinue Lisinopril and start Losartan$a16$, $b16$Stop lisinopril and discuss an ARB trial$b16$), explanation = $e16$Facial swelling a week after starting lisinopril is ACE-inhibitor angioedema. Stop the ACE inhibitor. Cross-reactivity if an ARB is later used is under 10%. An ARB can be considered only after discussing that risk, not as an automatic substitute, and he needs close monitoring. Continuing lisinopril, lowering the dose, or adding an antihistamine does not treat bradykinin angioedema.$e16$, "references" = $r16$[{"label": "Review of ACE-inhibitor angioedema (PMC8031276). Cross-reactivity with an ARB is under 10%, and starting an ARB after ACE-inhibitor angioedema requires a careful risk-benefit discussion.", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8031276/"}]$r16$::jsonb, manual_correction = true, "generationMeta" = CASE WHEN "generationMeta" IS NULL THEN '{"manualCorrection": true}'::jsonb WHEN jsonb_typeof("generationMeta")='object' THEN jsonb_set("generationMeta", '{manualCorrection}', 'true'::jsonb, true) ELSE "generationMeta" END, "updatedAt" = NOW()
WHERE id = 'cmruifog0001l1ycelduzbh95' AND "contentHash" = 'fff133d7db5349397894b60cd457e1c6af4c98625efde80e39efb17121d3577f';
UPDATE "QuestionBankItem" SET scenario = $s17$A boy born at 39 weeks is now 48 hours old and is breastfeeding. Total bilirubin is 17.2 mg/dL. There is no blood-group incompatibility, no hemolysis, no G6PD deficiency, and no signs of sepsis. He is feeding well and his vital signs are stable.$s17$, question = $q17$What is the appropriate next step?$q17$, "correctAnswer" = $k17$Start phototherapy$k17$, options = replace(options, $a17$Start phototherapy if above age-specific threshold; encourage feeds; follow bilirubin; check for hemolysis risk factors$a17$, $b17$Start phototherapy$b17$), explanation = $e17$At 48 hours of age, with no hyperbilirubinemia risk factors, the AAP 2022 phototherapy threshold is 16.6 mg/dL at 39 weeks (16.0 at 38 weeks and 17.0 at 40 weeks or more). His bilirubin is 17.2 mg/dL, so phototherapy is indicated. Exchange transfusion is for a much higher neurotoxicity threshold. He should keep feeding, not stop breastfeeding, and he should not be discharged without a plan.$e17$, "contentHash" = '0892b36dda2c05455cf247bab5569273b2ed163d8c84d3e6e021582c311bf3ae', manual_correction = true, "generationMeta" = CASE WHEN "generationMeta" IS NULL THEN '{"manualCorrection": true}'::jsonb WHEN jsonb_typeof("generationMeta")='object' THEN jsonb_set("generationMeta", '{manualCorrection}', 'true'::jsonb, true) ELSE "generationMeta" END, "updatedAt" = NOW()
WHERE id = 'cmrx1lugk001nl705dcpbs91q' AND "contentHash" = '96527dfb3f5ed7d8780764fec34d0f1ab24f8b53a3e850427badbbed7cf93065';
UPDATE "QuestionBankItem" SET scenario = $s18$A 2-year-old girl presents to the emergency department with a high fever of 102°F (38.9°C) and a rash that started on her face and spread down over her trunk. The mother reports that the child has been irritable and has had a runny nose for the past few days. On examination, the child has conjunctivitis and a maculopapular rash.$s18$, explanation = $e18$Fever, cough, coryza, conjunctivitis, and a maculopapular rash that starts on the head and moves down the body is measles. Rubella is milder. Roseola starts on the trunk after the fever breaks. Scarlet fever is a sandpaper rash with pharyngitis, not this cephalocaudal viral exanthem.$e18$, "references" = $r18$[{"label": "MedlinePlus. The measles rash often starts on the head and moves down the body, with fever, cough, runny nose, and conjunctivitis.", "url": "https://medlineplus.gov/measles.html"}]$r18$::jsonb, "contentHash" = '69297859520588e6cd3fde35f028026df7632c6acb76905de6165582e80831c1', manual_correction = true, "generationMeta" = CASE WHEN "generationMeta" IS NULL THEN '{"manualCorrection": true}'::jsonb WHEN jsonb_typeof("generationMeta")='object' THEN jsonb_set("generationMeta", '{manualCorrection}', 'true'::jsonb, true) ELSE "generationMeta" END, "updatedAt" = NOW()
WHERE id = 'cmr8n3pw800q01ygita18d8mz' AND "contentHash" = 'bb8df43df041362fe58a5c395fe71480f01ae6f412f647d7f162ea4ab8f7e7b8';
UPDATE "QuestionBankItem" SET scenario = $s19$A 72-year-old woman is admitted to the hospital with severe right hip pain after a fall at home. She has a history of osteoporosis and is currently on alendronate. On examination, her right leg is externally rotated and shortened. Her vital signs are stable, with a blood pressure of 130/80 mm Hg and heart rate of 78 bpm.$s19$, explanation = $e19$After a fall, a shortened and externally rotated leg in a woman with osteoporosis is a displaced femoral-neck fracture. The radiograph result is not stated. Hip dislocation more often follows a high-energy dashboard injury and the leg is usually flexed and internally rotated. Trochanteric and acetabular fractures have different deformity and mechanisms.$e19$, "contentHash" = '7c5f820a1dccbc8afde380d7185e7d2d4464de7aeba86f9f51d04c7a8e5ca9d5', manual_correction = true, "generationMeta" = CASE WHEN "generationMeta" IS NULL THEN '{"manualCorrection": true}'::jsonb WHEN jsonb_typeof("generationMeta")='object' THEN jsonb_set("generationMeta", '{manualCorrection}', 'true'::jsonb, true) ELSE "generationMeta" END, "updatedAt" = NOW()
